      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's an infected diabetic foot ulcer, and we'll know more once the blood tests is back. Let's book blood tests to look into infected ulcer. I'm going to order a wound swab, for infected ulcer. The treatment will be co-amoxiclav, 625 milligrams, three times a day, seven days. That's for infected ulcer. Keep the weight off the foot and keep the dressing dry.",
